  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Ruth",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "Elimelech and his family go to Moab because of famine—His sons marry—The father and sons die—Ruth, the Moabitess, her husband having died, remains constant to Naomi—They come to Bethlehem.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now it came to pass in the days when the judges ruled, that there was a famine in the land. And a certain man of Beth-lehem-judah went to sojourn in the country of Moab, he, and his wife, and his two sons.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "Judg. 2:16; Mosiah 29:44 (11–44)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:1",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And the name of the man was Elimelech, and the name of his wife Naomi, and the name of his two sons Mahlon and Chilion, Ephrathites of Beth-lehem-judah. And they came into the country of Moab, and continued there.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "HEB My God is king."
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "Gen. 35:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Gen. 35:19.",
            "prettyString": "Genesis 35:19",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "genesis",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 35,
                    "end": 35,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 19,
                        "end": 19
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:2",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And Elimelech Naomi’s husband died; and she was left, and her two sons.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:3",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And they took them wives of the women of Moab; the name of the one was Orpah, and the name of the other Ruth: and they dwelled there about ten years.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:4",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And Mahlon and Chilion died also both of them; and the woman was left of her two sons and her husband.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:5",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Then she arose with her daughters in law, that she might return from the country of Moab: for she had heard in the country of Moab how that the Lord had visited his people in giving them bread.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:6",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore she went forth out of the place where she was, and her two daughters in law with her; and they went on the way to return unto the land of Judah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:7",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And Naomi said unto her two daughters in law, Go, return each to her mother’s house: the Lord deal kindly with you, as ye have dealt with the dead, and with me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:8",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord grant you that ye may find rest, each of you in the house of her husband. Then she kissed them; and they lifted up their voice, and wept.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:9",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And they said unto her, Surely we will return with thee unto thy people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:10",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And Naomi said, Turn again, my daughters: why will ye go with me? are there yet any more sons in my womb, that they may be your husbands?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "Deut. 25:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 69
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 88
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Deut. 25:5.",
            "prettyString": "Deuteronomy 25:5",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "deuteronomy",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 25,
                    "end": 25,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 5,
                        "end": 5
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:11",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Turn again, my daughters, go your way; for I am too old to have an husband. If I should say, I have hope, if I should have an husband also to night, and should also bear sons;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 108
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:12",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Would ye tarry for them till they were grown? would ye stay for them from having husbands? nay, my daughters; for it grieveth me much for your sakes that the hand of the Lord is gone out against me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:13",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And they lifted up their voice, and wept again: and Orpah kissed her mother in law; but Ruth clave unto her.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "IE held fast to. TG Example."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:14",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And she said, Behold, thy sister in law is gone back unto her people, and unto her gods: return thou after thy sister in law.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ruth 1:15",
        "book": "Ruth",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ruth said, Entreat me not to leave thee, or to return from following after thee: for whither thou goest, I will go; and where thou lodgest, I will lodge: thy people shall be my people, and thy God my God:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "TG Family, Love within."
          },
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 118,
            "text": "TG Loyalty."
          },
          {
            "start": 162,
            "end": 168,
            "text": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood."
          },
          {
            "start": 204,
            "end": 207,
            "text": "TG Conversion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
